Do not think that I have come to abolish the Law or the Prophets. I have not come to abolish but to fulfill. For truly I say to you, until heaven and earth pass away, not one letter or one stroke of a letter will pass from the Law until all is accomplished.
What I am about to tell you is true. Heaven and earth will pass away, but not the smallest letter or stroke of the law will disappear until everything is accomplished.
Do not break even one of the least commandments. And teach others not to break them. For if you do this, you will be called the least important in the Kingdom of Heaven. But rather, do and teach these commandments. Then you will be called important in the Kingdom of Heaven.
Here is what I say to you. You must be more righteous than the Pharisees and the teachers of the law. If you are not, then you will surely not enter the kingdom of heaven. Murder
You have heard what was said to people long ago. It was said to them, " 'Do not murder.' (Exodus 20:13) Whoever murders will be judged to die."
Here is what I say to you. Do not be angry with your brother. Whoever is angry with his brother will be condemned. And again, whoever says to his brother: "You fool!" must be represented before the court in the Sanhedrin. But whoever says: "You are stupid!" will be in danger of facing the fires of hell.
Assume that you are offering your gift at the altar. And you remember that your brother has something against you.
Leave your gift before the altar. First, go and be reconciled with your brother. Then come and offer your gift.
Assume someone has a claim against you and takes you to court. Settle the matter quickly. Do this while you are still with him on your way. If you don't, he may hand you over to the judge. And the judge may hand you over to the officer. And you may be thrown into prison.
The thing I'm about to tell you is true. You will not leave until you pay the last penny! Adultery.
You have heard that it was said to the people long ago, "You shall not commit adultery."
But I tell you: whoever looks at a woman lustfully has already committed adultery with her in his heart.
If your right eye causes you to stumble, pluck it out and throw it away. For your right eye is only a part of your body. It is better for you to lose one part of your body than for your whole body to be thrown into hell."
If your right hand causes you to sin, cut it off and throw it away. For your hand alone has sinned. So it is better to lose a part of your body than for your whole body to be thrown into hell. Divorce.
It has been said, "When a man puts away his wife, let him give her a certificate of divorce." (Deuteronomy 24:1)
But this is what I tell you: whoever divorces his wife causes her to commit adultery; and whoever marries a divorced woman commits adultery. A man is allowed to divorce his wife if she is unfaithful to him. Oath
Again, you have heard what was said to your people long ago. It was said to them, "Do not break the covenants you make with the Lord your God. You shall not break your solemn vows, or delay fulfilling your pledges to God."
But here's what I say to you. Never make promises like that. Don't make them in heaven's name. That's God's throne.
Do not make it in the name of the land. That is the footstool of God. Do not make it in the name of Jerusalem. That is the city of the great King.
Do not swear by the name of your president. You cannot whiten or blacken even one hair.
Let your "yes" mean "yes," and your "no" mean "no." Anything more than this comes from the evil one. Be kind to one another.
I heard it said, "An eye for an eye, a tooth for a tooth." (Exodus 21:24; Leviticus 24:20; Deuteronomy 19:21)
But here is what I say to you. Do not resist evil. "Suppose someone strikes you on your right cheek. Turn to him your other cheek also.
Let's suppose someone takes you to court to get your shirt. Let him have your coat as well.
