Give what he asked of you. Do not go away from the one who wants to borrow something from you. Love your enemies.
I heard it said: "Love your neighbor and hate your enemy."
But this is what I tell you. Love your enemies. Pray for those who mistreat you.
Then you will be the sons of your Father who is in the heavens. "He causes His sun to rise on the evil and the good, and sends rain on the just and the unjust."
If you love those who love you, what reward will you get? Even the tax collectors do that.
If you greet one another, what more do you do than others? Even wrongdoers do that.
So be you also perfect, even as your Father which is in heaven is perfect.
Give to those in need.
Beware of doing your charitable deeds before men, to be seen by them. If you do that, your Father who is in heaven will not reward you.
When you give to the needy, do not announce it with trumpets. Do not be like those who pretend to be pious only. They announce their works in the temples and in the streets. They want to receive honor from others. What I am about to tell you is true. They have received their full reward.
When you give to the needy, do not let your left hand know what your right hand is doing.
Then your good deed done in secret will be rewarded by your Father who sees what you do in secret. Prayer.
When you pray, do not be like the hypocrites, who love to pray standing in the synagogues and on the street corners, so that they may be seen by others. I tell you the truth, they have received their full reward.
When you arrive, go into your room, close the door, and pray to your Father who cannot be seen. And He will reward you. Your Father sees what is done in secret.
And when you pray, do not lengthen your prayer like the nations who do not know Him, for they think that they will be heard because of their many words.
Don't be like them. Your father knows what you need, even before you ask him.
Thus you should pray: "Our Father who art in heaven, Hallowed be thy name.
Let your kingdom come. Let your will be done, as in heaven, so on earth.
Our Lord, give us every day our daily bread.
Forgive us our trespasses, as we also forgive those who trespass against us.
Deliver us from the fall into sin when we are dragged down. Save us from the devil.
Forgive people when they wrong you. If you do, then your Father who is in heaven will also forgive you.
And if you do not forgive people their sins, your father will not forgive your sins. Fasting.
When you go without eating, do not make your faces frown like those who only pretend to be pious. They make their faces very sad. They want to show people that they are fasting. What I am about to tell you is true. They have received their full reward.
But when you fast, do not look somber, but be cheerful.
So others will not know that you are fasting. Only your Father, who cannot be seen, will know. And He will reward you. Your Father sees what is done in secret. Lay up your treasures in heaven
Do not let wealth for yourselves be a hoard on earth. For the rust and moths can consume it. Burglars can break in and steal.
Instead of that, save the wealth for yourselves in the sky. There, it is not destroyed by moths nor by heads. There, it is not stormed by thieves nor is it stolen.
Your heart will be where your treasure is.
The eye is the lamp of the body. If your eyes are healthy, your whole body will be full of light.
But suppose your eyes are bad. Then your whole body will be full of darkness. If the light within you is darkness, it is very dark!
No one can serve two masters, for either he will hate the one and love the other, or he will be devoted to the one and despise the other. You cannot serve God and money. Therefore I tell you, do not be worried about your life, what you will eat or drink, or about your body, what you will wear. Is not life more than food, and the body more than clothing? Look at the birds in the sky: they do not sow or reap, they do not gather into barns, yet your heavenly Father feeds them. Are you not much more valuable than they?
I tell you: Do not worry. Do not worry about your life and about what you eat and drink. And do not worry about your bodies and about what you wear. Is not life more than food? And are not the things that are more important for the body more than clothes?
Look at the birds of the air: they neither sow nor reap, nor gather into barns; yet your heavenly Father feeds them. Are you not بالحري greater than they?
Can you add even one hour to your life by worrying?
And why do you worry about clothing? Observe the lilies of the field, how they grow; they do not toil, nor do they spin.
But here is what I say to you. Even Solomon in all his glory was not arrayed like one of those flowers.
If this is what God does with the wild grass, won't He clothe you in fine linen? For the grass is here today and tomorrow it will be thrown into the fire. Your faith is very small!
So do not worry. Do not say, 'What will we eat?' or 'What will we drink?' or 'What will we wear?'
Those who do not fear God seek after all these things. Your Father who is in heaven knows that you need them.
But seek first the kingdom of God and his righteousness. And all these things will be added to you.
So don't worry about tomorrow. Tomorrow will worry about itself. Every day has enough trouble of its own.
Be just when you judge others.
Do not judge, and you will not be judged.
You will be held accountable in the same manner that you hold others accountable. You will be measured in the same manner that you measure others.
You look at the speck of dust in your friend's eye, but you don't notice the wooden beam in your own eye.
How do you say to your friend, "Let me get that piece of wood out of your eye"? How do you say this when there is a piece of wood in your own eye?
O you who are claiming! First, take the beam out of your own eye. Then you will see well to take the splinter out of your friend's eye.
Do not give Jerusalem to the dogs, and do not throw your pearls before the swine; otherwise, they may trample them under their feet. Then, they may turn and tear you to pieces. Ask, seek, knock.
Ask and it will be given to you; seek and you will find; knock and it will be opened to you.
Let everyone who asks be given. And let everyone who seeks be found. And let the door be opened for everyone who knocks.
Let's suppose your son asked for bread. Which one of you would give him a stone?
Or let's suppose he asks for a fish. Which one of you will give him a snake?
Even though you are evil, you know how to give good gifts to your children. How much more will your Father in heaven give good things to those who ask him!
In everything, treat others as you would like to be treated. This is what is written in the Torah and the Prophets. The great and small doors.
Enter the kingdom of God through the narrow gate. The gate is wide and the road is spacious that leads to destruction, to hell. And many are those who enter through this road.
But the gate is small and the way is narrow that leads to life. And few find it. A tree and its fruit.
Beware of false prophets, who come to you in sheep's clothing, but inwardly are ravenous wolves.
You can know what they really are by what they do. "Do people pick grapes from bushes? Do they pick figs from thistles?
And on the same note, every good tree bears good fruit. But a corrupt tree bears corrupt fruit.
A good tree cannot bear bad fruit, nor can a bad tree bear good fruit.
Every tree that does not bear good fruit is cut down and thrown into the fire.
You can distinguish every tree by its fruits.
Not everyone who says to me, 'Lord, Lord,' will enter the kingdom of heaven, but only the one who does the will of my Father in heaven.
Many will say to me on that day: Lord, Lord, did we not prophesy in your name? And in your name we cast out demons? And in your name we performed many miracles? And then I will declare to them: I never knew you! Away from me, all you who are hypocrites!
Then I tell them clearly: 'I never knew you. Away from me, you evildoers!' The wise and foolish builders.
Therefore, everyone who hears my words and puts them into practice is like a wise man who built his house on the rock.
Rain falls. The water rises. The wind blows and beats against that house. But it does not fall. It is built on the rock.
But everyone who hears these words of mine and does not act on them will be like a foolish person who built his house on sand.
The rain fell. The water rose. The wind blew and hit that house. And it fell with a deafening roar."
Jesus finished speaking all these things. And the multitudes were amazed at his teachings.
He taught them as one who had authority, not like the teachers of the law.
Jesus heals a man with a skin disease.
Jesus came down from the mountain. A large crowd found him.
An ailing human with leprosy came and knelt before Jesus, saying, "Lord, if you are willing to cleanse me, then you have the power to do so."
Jesus stretched out his hand and touched the man. "I am willing to do so," he said. "Be 'clean'!" Immediately the man was healed from the skin disease.
Then Jesus said to him, "Do not tell anyone, but go and show yourself to the priest and offer the sacrifice that Moses commanded, as a testimony to them." A Roman centurion believed.
And when Jesus entered the city of Capernaum, a Roman centurion came to him. And he asked him, saying, Lord, come down before my servant dies.
"Lord," he said, "my servant is lying in the house, unable to move. He is suffering severely."
Jesus said, "I will go and heal him."
The captain answered, "Sir, I am not worthy to have you enter under my roof. But just say the word, and my servant will be healed.
I myself am a man subject to authority. And I have soldiers who obey my orders. I say to this one, "Go," and he goes. And I say to that one, "Come," and he comes. And I say to my servant, "Do this," and he does it."
When Jesus heard this, he was amazed and said to those who were following him, "Truly I tell you, I have not found such great faith, even in Israel."
I tell you that many will come from the east and the west, and they will sit down to eat together in the kingdom of heaven. They will be sitting down with Abraham and Isaac and Jacob in the kingdom of heaven.
