Then Jesus said to the Roman centurion, "Go! It will be done just as you believed it would." And his servant was healed at that very hour. Jesus heals many people.
When Jesus came to Peter's house, he saw Peter's mother-in-law lying in bed. She was suffering from a fever.
Jesus touched her hand, and the fever left her. She got up and began waiting on Him.
And in the evening, those who were possessed by unclean spirits were brought to Jesus, and he cast out those spirits with a word. And he healed all the sick.
He did it to fulfill what the prophet Isaiah said. He said, "He suffered the things that we should have suffered. He took upon himself the diseases that we should have had." (Isaiah 53:4) Following Jesus has costs.
